messages:
greta: Opened a docs PR (gh#5066) to standardize function/tool-calling examples and repair a few broken anchors after the restructure. Main asks: pick a canonical wrapper shape, add minimal Python/Node SDK snippets + a tiny parse-fallback, and sweep stale anchors on the site.
ishan: Can you paste the PR link and list the failing anchors?
greta: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5066 \u2014 failing anchors: /docs/tooling#schema-examples -> should be /docs/tooling#schema-examples-stable, and /docs/structured-output#json-shape -> header id moved. I put details in the PR description.
zoe: I looked through examplesthere are three patterns: flat (top-level), wrapper called "envelope", and a compact wrapper. My vote: use a short, neutral name `tool_packet` to avoid colliding with other libs. Keeps metadata isolated.
priya: `tool_packet` sounds good. We should publish a minimal JSON Schema and 1-line migration snippet showing parse_tool_packet_fallback(). Also call out nullable arrays and null params as a common parsing pitfall.
ishan: Draft schema suggestion:
```
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool_packet": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "payload": {"type": ["object", "array", "null"]}
      },
      "required": ["name"]
    }
  },
  "required": ["tool_packet"]
}
```
zoe: Nice. I'll add two compact snippets under docs/snippets/tool_packet: python.md and node.md. Each will show generate + parse_tool_packet_fallback(). Keep them tiny (6-8 lines).
priya: I'll update the main call-calling page to recommend `tool_packet` as canonical and include a short migration blurb: "Switch to the `tool_packet` wrapper for forward compatibility. Use parse_tool_packet_fallback() to accept legacy flat responses during rollout."
greta: For anchors: is someone able to run a grep+replace across the markdown and the built HTML to update old anchors to the stable kebab-case ids? We should also add a link-checker rule that fails on header ids containing backticks or parentheses.
ishan: I can run the sweep and open a tiny follow-up PR to update anchors and add a test in the link-check job. Estimated ~30-45m. I'll also normalize header-id generation in the build script to strip punctuation.
zoe: I'll push snippets in ~2 hours and add the parse shim example:
```
# Node pseudo
const res = await client.generate({input: 'call', structured_output: {schema: TOOL_PACKET_SCHEMA_ID}})
const obj = parse_tool_packet_fallback(res.text)
if (obj.tool_packet) await runTool(obj.tool_packet.name, obj.tool_packet.payload)
else await runTool(obj.name, obj.payload)
```
priya: Small migration note about arrays: sometimes models return null for lists. Example: `results: null` vs `results: []`. Recommend callers treat both as empty lists when safe. I'll add that as a one-liner in the FAQ.
greta: Great. Action items I tracked: zoe -> snippets + parse shim; ishan -> anchor sweep + link-check tweak; priya -> migration blurb + nullable-array note; greta -> review + merge after link-check passes.
docs-bot: Deploy to staging: successful 1 link-check job queued.
ishan: I'll wait for zoe's push then run link-check locally. Tagging @greta once green.
greta: Thanks all. Merge once link-check is green and snippets are in. :thumbsup:
